It's no secret that Nitrous.IO has been making it easy for developers to start new projects with our instantly provisioned development workspaces for a variety of languages.
Today, We're excited to announce that we're taking that to the next level with the launch of Nitrous.IO Hack button.

The *Hack* button makes any OSS project, tutorial or sample app immediately available in a fully functional linux workspace allowing developers to start hacking on their favorite code in seconds.
This means that you can start contributing to OSS projects such as (Grape), start building your next startup with apps from [Rails Apps]() integrate technology from leading developer companies such as [Twilio] and [Sendgrid] or even follow along on tutorial from [learnable]() or [Discover Meteor] by running the code yourself.


Leading developers at these partners have already deployed the Hack button:

    SendGrid
    Firebase
    Learnable/Sitepoint
    O'Reilly Media
    Meteor
    Discover Meteor
    Rails Apps
    Twilio



Read more about why our partners love the Hack button and find out how [you can join the movement.](http://nitrous.io/embed/?{{page.utm}})

